From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] scripts/setup: exclude gn/ninja/clang from the Pigweed CIPD
 fetch on riscv64

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [riscv64 CI infra choice: gn/ninja/clang come from this repo's build-skia-python.yml precedent instead of CIPD, not a bug in gen_pigweed_cipd_json.py]

fuchsia/third_party/ninja has no linux-riscv64 CIPD build at all (404
against the live backend, confirmed at the pinned git_revision), and
while gn/gn and fuchsia/third_party/clang both do, chip_python_wheel_action
only runs Python scripts (build-chip-wheel.py) and nothing in
BUILD.gn/python_wheel.gni references clang or protoc directly, so
clang is unnecessary for this build. Reuse the mechanism this file
already uses to keep fuchsia/third_party/rust/ and
infra/3pp/tools/renode out of the generated CIPD package list, instead
of relying on CIPD's riscv64 coverage (or lack of it) for these three
tools: gn is built from source and ninja comes from its own riscv64
PyPI wheel, exactly as this repo's build-skia-python.yml/
build-skia-pathops.yml already do for the same gn/Ninja GN-based
family, put on PATH ahead of bootstrap.sh.

This script runs on both the x86_64 build_prepare job (ZAP codegen,
which genuinely needs gn/ninja/clang from CIPD) and the riscv64
build_wheels job (which carries over the same patched checkout and
runs its own bootstrap.sh), so the three riscv64-only exclusions are
gated on `platform.machine() == 'riscv64'` rather than applied
unconditionally; the pre-existing rust/renode exclusions are left
unconditional since they are unrelated to riscv64.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 scripts/setup/gen_pigweed_cipd_json.py | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/scripts/setup/gen_pigweed_cipd_json.py b/scripts/setup/gen_pigweed_cipd_json.py
index 4fe77aa..8ee7478 100644
--- a/scripts/setup/gen_pigweed_cipd_json.py
+++ b/scripts/setup/gen_pigweed_cipd_json.py
@@ -25,6 +25,13 @@ _LIST_OF_PACKAGES_TO_EXCLUDE = {
     'infra/3pp/tools/renode',
 }

+if platform.machine() == 'riscv64':
+    _LIST_OF_PACKAGES_TO_EXCLUDE.update({
+        'gn/gn/',
+        'fuchsia/third_party/ninja/',
+        'fuchsia/third_party/clang/',
+    })
+

 def include_package(package: dict) -> bool:
     if 'path' in package:
